Build a small website for field hockey with TWO pages:

1) index.html (one-page editorial landing)
2) skills.html (interactive coaching + practice toolkit)

Create these files:
- index.html
- skills.html
- styles.css
- skills.js
- README.md

Design + tone:
- Editorial, minimal, premium sports vibe.
- Neutral palette, strong typography, lots of whitespace.
- Responsive and clean.

index.html requirements (one-page):
- Sections with anchors: Hero, About, Playing, Coaching, Contact.
- A prominent button/link in the header and hero: “Skills & Drills” that navigates to skills.html.
- Copy should be polished English and athletic (not cheesy).
- Include a small “quick stats” row (e.g., roles, focus areas, location) using simple cards.

skills.html requirements (interactive):
- Use the SAME header/nav style as index.html.
- Include a “Back to Home” link (index.html).
- Interactive toolkit with:
  A) Drill Library (filterable)
     - Filters: Skill (Passing / Receiving / Press break / Scanning / Wide-middle), Level (Beginner/Intermediate/Advanced), Time (10/20/30 min)
     - Show drill cards dynamically based on filters
  B) Drill Detail Modal or Expandable Card
     - Each drill shows: objective, setup, steps, coaching cues, progression, common mistakes
  C) Practice Timer
     - 10/20/30 minute preset buttons + Start/Pause/Reset
     - Display remaining time
  D) Session Builder (simple)
     - “Add to session” button on drills
     - Session list appears on the right or bottom
     - Ability to remove drills + show estimated total time

Seed content (include at least 8 drills):
- Include drills inspired by this coaching idea:
  “Routes starting from the 16’ with faster decision-making; press into defenders, create a passing route between them, keep the ball on our side to move the press, then find the wide-middle channel.”
- Make sure at least 3 drills are about:
  - connecting defenders under press
  - moving the press with patience
  - finding the wide-middle space

Technical:
- No frameworks. Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS only.
- skills.html should load skills.js.
- Keep code well-structured and commented.
- Make sure GitHub Pages works (relative paths only).
- Commit everything in a single pull request.

README.md:
- Explain the two pages and how to deploy on GitHub Pages.
